### Query params - basic

GET https://httpbin.org/get?name=John
  &age=30 HTTP/1.1

### Query params - single digit value

GET https://httpbin.org/get?id=1 HTTP/1.1

### Query params - special chars in name

GET https://httpbin.org/get?user_id=123
  &email@domain=test HTTP/1.1

### Query params - special chars in value

GET https://httpbin.org/get?path=/api/v1
  &url=http://example.com
  &port=8080 HTTP/1.1

### Query params - underscores, hyphens, dots

GET https://httpbin.org/get?user_name=john
  &api-key=abc123
  &file.name=test.txt HTTP/1.1

### Query params - all valid chars

GET https://httpbin.org/get?a_b-c.d=x_y-z.w
  &email=user@example.com
  &path=/api/v1:8080 HTTP/1.1

### Query params - no value before HTTP

GET https://httpbin.org/get?param HTTP/1.1

### Query params - value before HTTP

GET https://httpbin.org/get?param=value HTTP/1.1

### Query params with spaces

GET https://echo.getkulala.net/get?id=123
  &value=some "longer" content HTTP/1.1

### Query params without HTTP version

GET https://httpbin.org/get?name=John
  &age=30 HTTP/1.1

### Query params with spaces, no HTTP version

GET https://echo.getkulala.net/get?id=123
  &value=some "longer" content HTTP/1.1

### Query params multiline

GET https://httpbin.org/get
  ?name=John
  &age=30 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json HTTP/1.1

### Query params with spaces multiline

GET https://echo.getkulala.net/get
  ?id=123
  &value=some "longer" content HTTP/1.1

### Query params multiline 2

GET https://echo.getkulala.net/get
  ?id=1
  &va_lue=so_me "longer" content
  &extra=1
 # fragment HTTP/1.1
  HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

### Query with variables

@some_param = userId
@some_var = 42

GET https://postman-echo.com/get
  ?{{some_param}}={{some_var}} HTTP/1.1

### Form params

POST https://httpbin.org/post HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&
username=foo&
password=bar&
client_id=foo

### POST with query params in body

POST https://api.example.com/endpoint HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=John&
age=30&
city=NewYork

### Form with variables

@pass = secret123
@user = admin

POST https://api.example.com/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{user}}&
password={{pass}}&
remember=true

### Form with empty values

POST https://api.example.com/form HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

field1=&
field2=value&
field3=

### Form with special chars

POST https://api.example.com/data HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email=user@example.com&
tags=test,prod&
path=/api/v1

### Request

POST http://httpbin.org/users/post
  ?param1=value1
  &param2=value2
 # fragment HTTP/1.1
  HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "results": [
    {
      "desc": "some_username",
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "desc": "another_username",
      "id": 2
    }
  ]
}

> {%
  client.log(client.global.test)
  client.global.test = "test value"
  client.log(client.global.test)
%}

### File Upload

@content_type = image/jpeg
@filename = logo.png
@filepath = ../../assets/badge-discord.svg

POST https://httpbin.org/post HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary{{$timestamp}}

------WebKitFormBoundary{{$timestamp}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="field1"
Content-Type: text/plain

Value for field1
------WebKitFormBoundary{{$timestamp}}
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="field2"
Content-Type: text/plain

Value for field2
------WebKitFormBoundary{{$timestamp}}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="{{filename}}"
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

< {{filepath}}

------WebKitFormBoundary{{$timestamp}}--

### Test multipart with multiple parts and inline content

@filepath = ../../assets/badge-discord.svg

POST https://httpbin.org/post HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="field1"
Content-Type: text/plain

Value for field1
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="field2"
Content-Type: text/plain

Value for field2
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="image.jpeg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< {{filepath}}

--boundary123--

